Actually, no.

This is one of the particular quirks of English, which I also had
trouble mastering. Singular words that indicate a plural thing (a group)
have a verb that is plural. The most common example is "The police ARE".

This is something that is very counterintuitive to non-native speakers,
but the original poster was quite right.

I don't know if there are any other languages besides English that treat
singular words with a plural meaning like that as well.

